2026-10-26  0.1.0 (development)

- Initial C11 evaluator and public spy_* embedding API.
- Reference counting with iterative destruction and explicit cycle collection.
- Functions, closures, control flow, containers, host-loaded modules.
- spy command-line host and spyc standalone C source generator.
- Local semantic checks, upstream Cython adapter, versioned language target.
- Pinned CPython 3.15 development oracle, complete test-file ledger, isolated
  unittest discovery, and upstream unpacking/comprehension doctest ports.
- Nested/starred unpacking, chained assignment, comprehension scopes, lazy
  generator expressions, and Python 3.15 starred comprehension elements.
- Defaults, positional-only/keyword-only parameters, variadic arguments,
  keyword calls, lambdas, and assignment expressions.
- Basic classes, bound methods, exception handling, context managers, deletion,
  builtin type objects, stateful iterators, and sets.
- Code objects, module-scope eval/exec, string joining, and partial formatting.
- Generator functions with owned suspension stacks, send/throw/close, yield
  delegation, return values, and exception/context-manager cleanup.
- List/tuple/string slices, slice assignment/deletion, and index conversion.
- print keyword arguments, Python file objects, and a host flush callback.
- Upstream CPython generator doctests and suspended-stack ownership checks.
- Static scope validation, global/nonlocal bindings, private-name mangling,
  decorators, static/class methods, properties, and user-defined descriptors.
- Named string-format fields, function-scope locals, and partial dir support.
- Interactive expression display, runtime Cython doctest discovery, and all
  CPython syntax doctests in the adapted selection.
- Function metadata, live globals/module dictionaries, local snapshots, and
  explicit eval/exec namespaces with custom builtins.
- F-strings, debug fields, conversions, nested format specifications, and
  suspension while evaluating formatted strings.
- Complex literals, construction, conversion hooks, arithmetic, and signed-zero
  handling for mixed real/complex operations.
- NotImplemented and Ellipsis, all augmented-assignment operators, reflected
  arithmetic dispatch, and in-place list extension/repetition.
- Complete unchanged CPython decorator and augmented-assignment unittest modules
  through a test-only framework adapter; the integer-literal module extends
  the passing selection, together with unary operators, to 35 cases.
- Unicode 17.0.0 printable properties and escaping, checked across every code
  point; string splitlines and isprintable.
- Arbitrary-precision integers with exact comparison, signed bit operations,
  floor division, float rounding, modular powers/inverses, bit counts, large
  enumerate counters, and checked fixed-width C API access.
- Immutable bytes literals, construction, sequence operations, and binary C API.
- Native coroutines, await delegation, asynchronous iteration/context managers,
  asynchronous generators, asend/athrow/aclose, and aiter/anext builtins.
- Exception context preservation across suspended cleanup and cycle checks for
  coroutine wrappers, async-generator operations, and pending async exits.
- Shared comprehension execution with async clauses, awaited elements/filters,
  and lazy async generator expressions; 120 async operation-state checks.
- Package/relative imports, multiple imports, import hooks, the builtins namespace
  module, and parenthesized synchronous/asynchronous context managers.
- Arbitrary-precision ranges, range indexing/slicing/reversal and equality,
  count/index methods, and arbitrary-precision slice normalization.
- Rich comparison methods, reflected subclass priority, non-boolean results,
  containment hooks, implicit unhashability, and mutation-safe comparison paths.
- Writable function defaults, retained code metadata, stable sorting keys and
  reverse ordering, and single-statement compilation with expression display.
- Assignment-expression grammar and comprehension diagnostics; complete unchanged
  keyword-only and assignment-expression modules extend the passing selection to
  120 cases and 99 subtests. The adapter checks subtest outcomes against CPython.
- Slice equality/ordering share the tuple/list comparison implementation.
- List extension, insertion, removal, clearing, copying, reversal, counting,
  indexing, and in-place sorting with callback mutation detection. The unchanged
  large-expression module extends the passing upstream selection to 121 cases.
- Explicit exception causes, context suppression, cause validation, and suspension
  in raise expressions; assertions preserve message objects and evaluation order.
- All 194 upstream call doctests, keyword validation order, full missing-argument
  diagnostics, and 560 supplementary argument-binding checks.
- This release does not claim full Python 3.15 or Cython compatibility.
- Class allocator dispatch, implicit static wrapping of __new__, initialization
  of returned subclasses, and 288 supplementary construction checks.
- Shared attribute deletion and delattr, including function-default removal.
- User-defined hashing, cached dictionary entry hashes and tuple hashes,
  numeric hash consistency, and 913 supplementary hash comparisons.
- Dictionary copy, clear, pop, popitem and setdefault, with stored-hash reuse
  during copying, equality and updates. Missing-key exceptions retain the key.
- Unicode 17 identifier syntax, NFKC normalization and strict source UTF-8;
  exhaustive identifier properties and 297,124 source-normalization checks.
- Unicode filenames in the command-line host's module loader. Upstream report
  fingerprints now include generated Unicode data and host-loader source.
- SyntaxError metadata and location formatting; all three unchanged Unicode
  identifier cases now pass. The strict unittest selection has 124 cases.
- Test-only module search reaches pinned upstream dependencies and fixtures,
  with package/module precedence checked across search directories.
- Exact decimal rounding for integers and floats, ties to even, signed zero,
  __round__ dispatch, and 5,238 supplementary numeric rounding checks.
- C3 multiple inheritance, explicit and zero-argument super, lexical class
  cells, class construction hooks and exception notes. Class headers reuse
  call argument parsing; three-argument type shares class finalization.
- 240 supplementary inheritance hierarchies plus callback, descriptor mutation,
  class cell, super binding, and cyclic ownership checks.
- Class subscription hooks, type.mro, property naming, and instance attribute
  interception with explicit object-method delegation.
- Shared str/bytes prefix, suffix, forward/reverse search, index and count
  methods, with Unicode positions and tuple-prefix short circuiting; 286
  upstream-derived literal examples and 5,600 differential search cases.
- Shared definition code objects and generator/coroutine/async-generator code
  attributes retained after closure, with source-unit cache cycle tracing.
- Metaclass namespace mappings and callable __prepare__, custom mro methods,
  class first-line/static-attribute metadata, and shared exec/eval mapping locals.
- All 73 unchanged upstream metaclass doctest examples pass. The unchanged
  exception-variation module adds 30 passing cases, bringing the strict whole-
  module selection to 154 cases in nine modules, plus 99 subtests.
- Native C template strings preserve interpolation values, source spelling,
  conversions, and evaluated format specifications. Constructors, concatenation,
  iteration, matching and suspended fields share normal runtime ownership.
  Checks cover 336 literals and all 21 upstream malformed-template table entries.
- Oracle runners exclude the local tests directory from dependency lookup so
  numbers.py cannot shadow CPython's standard-library module.
- Upstream report fingerprints include embedded intrinsic source and generated
  data. The manual distinguishes that Python implementation from the C11 goal.
- String-subclass keyword names retain their identities in **kwargs and use
  rich comparison when binding Python parameters. Call-unpacking diagnostics
  distinguish absent protocols from errors raised inside user methods.
- Current CPython doctests: 1,347 passed, 88 failed out of 1,435. Cython static
  doctests: 343 passed, 11,107 failed; dynamic: 367 passed, 11,176 failed.
- Bytearray mutation rechecks storage after index/value conversions; scalar
  and extended-slice deletion share assignment handling. Empty reverse slices
  and empty extended-slice replacement no longer reach invalid memory.
- Bytearray resize and Python 3.15 take_bytes, with conversion-mutation checks
  derived from the upstream bytearray regressions.
- Shared builtin argument parsing safely rejects missing positional arguments
  and unexpected keywords when no keyword-name table exists.
- Semantic tests prefer the pinned 3.15 oracle. Pattern diagnostics, type-alias
  display inside aliases/unions, and object descriptor repr follow that version.
- Bounded per-context small-tuple storage reuse makes the upstream generator
  tuple-reuse example independent of host malloc behavior. Cached allocations
  retain no elements and are released with the context.
- Upstream driver reports actual error filenames and lines, including imported
  dependencies. The object/bytearray module attempt accounts for 635 failures.
- Builtin method descriptors and slot wrappers (list.append, int.__add__,
  object.__repr__, ...) with CPython names, reprs, and argument diagnostics;
  in-place slot wrappers update their operand.
- Live dict_keys, dict_values, and dict_items views: set operations and
  comparisons, membership, reversal, isdisjoint, mapping proxies, and
  size-change detection. reversed() accepts dictionaries.
- Iterators have CPython's classes (list_iterator, dict_keyiterator,
  callable_iterator, ...) with __next__/__iter__ slot wrappers; map, zip,
  enumerate, filter, and reversed are builtin classes. iter(callable,
  sentinel), zip(strict=True), and enumerate keywords follow CPython.
- object.__subclasshook__; slot wrappers report CPython's "requires" error.
- Complete printf-style % formatting for str, bytes, and bytearray, ported
  from CPython's formatter with its 3.15 diagnostics. Sequence subscripts
  report CPython's per-type TypeError and IndexError messages.
- Format-spec mini-language ported from CPython's unicode_formatter.c and
  short float repr: grouping (including fractional), z, n, c, complex specs,
  Unicode fill and width digits, and CPython's error messages.
- str.format and str.format_map ported from CPython's unicode_format.h:
  field paths ({0[1]}, {0.attr}), nested specs, mapping lookups through
  __getitem__/__missing__, and CPython's messages.
- CPython's SyntaxError and IndentationError messages for malformed parameter
  lists, incompatible string prefixes, unbalanced brackets, missing indented
  blocks, conditional expressions, and duplicate parameters; compiler-stage
  errors (break/continue/return/yield/await/async placement) are deferred until
  the source parses.
- CPython's assignment-target diagnostics: "cannot assign to/delete X",
  "... here. Maybe you meant '==' instead of '='?", augmented-assignment,
  assert, call keyword and starred-argument messages.
- Minimal built-in modules collections, types, and weakref, embedded from
  modules/ and parsed on first import without a host loader. Weak references
  use a context weak table cleared on release and by the cycle collector;
  callbacks run at the next statement boundary. Also module(name, doc) and
  method(function, instance) constructors, property() keyword arguments, and
  reversed() over __reversed__ and the sequence protocol.
- Numeric tokenization, incomplete-input handling, parser error spans and
  invalid-expression diagnostics follow the pinned Python 3.15 tests. Traceback
  keyword suggestions use spy_error_display without changing the raw exception.
  All 552 syntax doctests that do not require ast now pass; the remaining ast
  example stays recorded as a failure.
- Mapping proxies moved from embedded Python into C. Class dictionaries and
  dictionary views share live read-only proxies; reflected equality callbacks
  receive copies of exact dictionaries as required by Python 3.15. Explicit
  dict.__getitem__ preserves subclass __missing__, including slice keys.
- Upstream reports fingerprint modules/*.py as well as the generated header.
- Generator, coroutine and async-generator names retain the creating function's
  current metadata. Qualified names drive repr and survive closure; string
  subclasses and cycles are retained correctly. Python 3.15 gi_state and cr_state
  now share the existing async-generator state handling.
- Native Python 3.15 frozendict: construction and subclasses, views, merging,
  matching, cached item-pair hashing, copying and fromkeys. Frozen eval/exec
  globals and builtins remain read-only; type() accepts frozen namespaces.
  Eleven unchanged upstream methods supplement the whole-module test ledger.
- Doctest output comparison follows CPython's trailing-newline normalization;
  raw captured output stays unchanged in reports.
- Complete unchanged type-check and subclass-initialization unittest modules;
  the selection now passes 177 cases in eleven modules, plus 99 subtests.
  Test-only regex and multiset assertions are checked against CPython.
- Native byte-source decoding for compile/eval/exec, CLI and module loading,
  with encoding comments, BOMs, CR/CRLF normalization and ISO-8859-15.
  Tab indentation uses Python column and consistency rules. The whole-module
  selection now passes 180 cases in twelve modules; six unchanged encoding
  methods and 789 oracle comparisons supplement it.
- Parser diagnostics carry CPython's column ranges for raise/from, import,
  except and pattern targets, misplaced 'not', and unparenthesized generator
  arguments. Unterminated strings and unclosed brackets report CPython's
  offsets. Compiler errors inside f-string fields are no longer lost, and an
  await expression reports the line of its keyword.
- Built-in sys module: modules, exception/exc_info, recursion and integer
  string-conversion limits, host stdout/stderr used by print, and constant
  metadata struct sequences. Python frames count against the recursion limit;
  C recursion is bounded by a stack budget with CPython's messages.
- Python 3.15 lazy imports (PEP 810) with placeholder reification, resolution
  cause chaining, and the parser's placement errors; types.LazyImportType.
- A test.support adapter and a backtracking regex subset, skip decorators,
  and expected failures in the test-only unittest replacement.
- property, classmethod and staticmethod are subclassable and expose their
  descriptor methods; property errors name the property and owner type.
- sys._getframe frames with write-through FrameLocalsProxy f_locals,
  sys._getframemodulename, types.FrameType, type.__subclasses__, and a
  built-in _weakref module.
- memoryview over bytes, bytearray and __buffer__ objects, with native
  formats, casts, slicing and bytearray export locking; bytes consumers
  accept buffers.
- collections is a package whose abc submodule is _collections_abc; module
  __getattr__ (PEP 562); imports return the final sys.modules entry.
- ImportError name/path/name_from/msg, AttributeError name/obj and NameError
  name, filled by failed lookups; CPython's unbound-local and from-import
  messages.
- Built-in itertools module following CPython's C implementation.
- sentinel builtin (PEP 661), built-in _thread for the single engine thread,
  object.__reduce__/__reduce_ex__/__getstate__, builtin __self__, and
  CPython's read-only attribute and ordering messages.
- Built-in gc and _typing modules; __get__ on functions, methods and method
  descriptors; builtin slots take MRO precedence over later Python bases.
- isinstance/issubclass follow CPython's abstract __bases__ protocol.
- Sequence repetition (operators and the __mul__/__rmul__/__imul__ wrappers)
  accepts any __index__ object; int subclasses index directly, as
  PyNumber_Index; CPython's int-conversion and bad-__index__ messages.
- Named Unicode escapes (\N{...}) from generated Unicode 17.0.0 name and
  alias tables; f-string conversions and debug '=' fields allow trailing
  whitespace and comments.
- Closure cells: __closure__, co_freevars/co_cellvars, types.CellType;
  global declarations in nested scopes make the module-level name global.
- __del__ finalizers run once, after release or collection, at the next
  statement boundary; resurrection is honored and exceptions are discarded.
- Membership tests on non-containers report "argument of type 'X' is not a
  container or iterable".
- builtins: __build_class__, __lazy_import__, breakpoint, exit, quit,
  ImportCycleError, _IncompleteInputError, and the module's True/False/None,
  __debug__, __doc__, __package__, __loader__, and __spec__. SystemExit.code;
  spy exits with it. CPython argument-count and keyword messages for builtins;
  keywords for compile, eval, exec, and complex; builtin iterator reprs.
- types.FunctionType(code, globals, ...); exec/eval of function code objects,
  with exec's closure keyword.
- C API: spy_native, spy_call_keywords, spy_tuple, spy_dict, spy_get_item,
  spy_set_item, spy_get_attr, spy_set_attr, spy_iter, spy_next, spy_str,
  spy_error_value, and spy_raise.
- The core no longer contains standard modules. spy_new_module and
  spy_exec_module register modules QuickJS-style; the standard layer
  spy-std.c (libspy-std.a, spy_std_init) provides sys, gc, weakref, types,
  itertools, collections, _thread, and _typing on the core's _spy primitives.
- spy_set_opaque/spy_get_opaque attach a host pointer to a context.
- smallpython Python package (python/smallpython, setup.py): a CPython
  extension embedding the engine. Runtime eval/exec/call, globals as items,
  Python callables as host functions with keywords, registered modules,
  Object wrappers, value conversion, and exception mapping both ways.
- match subjects accept unparenthesized walrus items (match w := x, :).
- Traceback objects: __traceback__ chains built as an error leaves each frame,
  tb_next/tb_frame/tb_lineno/tb_lasti, types.TracebackType, with_traceback,
  and tracebacks passed to __exit__ and accepted by generator throw().
- open() in the core with _io-style file objects, reaching only host
  directories mounted with spy_mount (read-only mounts, realpath and
  O_NOFOLLOW containment, context-owned descriptors). spy mounts its working
  directory by default and takes --mount; the binding has Runtime.mount.
- OSError(errno, strerror, filename, ...) selects the errno subclass and sets
  errno, strerror, filename, filename2, and characters_written.
- Errors raised inside intrinsic code report the caller's location and add no
  traceback entries.
- Built-in iterators' __length_hint__ (sequence, dict, set, range, reversed),
  and PyObject_LengthHint error propagation in list(), list.extend, and
  bytearray.extend.
- Exception fields live outside the instance __dict__ as C members do, with
  CPython's deletion rules; read-only group message/exceptions; groups over
  any sequence with the saved repr; BaseException/OSError/ImportError/
  AttributeError __reduce__, __setstate__, and __getstate__; Unicode error
  fields, constructor checks, and str; codec errors carry their fields.
- __repr__/__str__ returning a non-str raise CPython 3.15's message.
- Recursive-repr detection is per context (Py_ReprEnter), so a container
  reached again through a user __repr__ prints as [...] or {...}; deep
  containers raise RecursionError instead of a fixed 128-level limit.
- collections' UserDict, OrderedDict, and defaultdict | accept frozendict.
- Exception fields are member_descriptor/getset_descriptor objects in the
  builtin exception classes.
- __slots__: sorted, name-mangled member descriptors, instances without a
  __dict__, and CPython's slot validation and layout-conflict errors.
- CPython unittest ports add test_contains, test_exception_group,
  test_iterlen, and test_userdict (322 cases in 18 modules).
- Future statements: placement and feature checks, barry_as_FLUFL and
  CO_FUTURE_BARRY_AS_BDFL with the '<>' operator; the statement runs without
  a __future__ module. Compiler-phase errors in strings have text None.
- A comparison's result is tested for truth only between chained comparisons.
- test.support's recursion and digit limit helpers also decorate functions.
- PEP 563: from __future__ import annotations stores annotations as strings
  in CPython's unparsed form; module and class bodies fill __annotations__
  as they run. compile/exec/eval inherit the caller's future flags.
- Class __name__/__qualname__ live outside the class __dict__; classes get
  CPython's __dict__ and __weakref__ getset descriptors.
- object.__new__ refuses classes with __abstractmethods__.
- CPython's nesting limits: 200 brackets, MemoryError for parser stack
  overflow, iterative prefix-operator runs, and stack-bounded compiler checks
  (long expressions such as 400 additions compile).
- Language specification tests (tests/spec, make test-spec): test262-style
  files per Language Reference section, validated on the oracle.
- Compound statements are refused in a suite on the same line as its header;
  method objects compare and hash by self and function; dir() honours a
  module's __dir__ and a metaclass __dir__.
- __class__ assignment between Python classes with the same layout, with
  CPython's errors.
- Builtin types are immutable; their __dict__ and dir() list the method,
  getset and member descriptors (int.real, range.start, property.fget,
  classmethod.__func__); class.__type_params__ defaults to ().
- object.__dir__, object.__sizeof__, type.__dir__, type.__instancecheck__,
  type.__subclasscheck__, type.__or__/__ror__; a class's own methods take
  priority over its metaclass's non-data descriptors.
- bytes/bytearray splitlines and maketrans, float/complex from_number,
  __getnewargs__, range.__bool__, enumerate/slice/memoryview generics.
- nonlocal cannot bind a type parameter.
- PEP 420 namespace packages through a loader "name.__namespace__" probe;
  modules record __file__; star imports check __all__ items and import a
  package's listed submodules.
- Spec tests can ship fixture modules in a sibling NAME.fixtures directory.
- co_varnames orders *args and **kwargs after named parameters; str.split
  keeps the remainder's whitespace after maxsplit; sum() compensates float
  rounding and rejects str/bytes start values.
- eval() syntax errors locate the error in the input and skip leading blanks.
- CPython's wording for method arity, unary/len/iter/subscript type errors,
  zero powers, float overflow, unhashable dict keys and set elements, empty
  set pop, division by zero, eval/exec/format/open argument errors, and
  dict.pop on an empty dict raises before hashing the key.
- input() through a host line reader (spy_set_input); map(strict=True);
  plain object() instances have no __dict__; with statements name the
  missing context manager method.
- Spec tests for compound control flow (loops with else, try/finally,
  except*, with) and the built-in functions.
- compile(optimize>=1) drops assert statements and makes __debug__ False;
  a bad __await__ result names the awaited type.
- Spec tests for built-in type methods, primaries and evaluation order,
  top-level components, and object identity, equality, and hashing.
- The buffer protocol (PEP 688): objects with __buffer__ work in bytes(),
  bytearray(), concatenation, join, and bytes searches; str and bytes
  subclasses are accepted as search needles.
- object.__repr__ uses the qualified name and omits the builtins module;
  type() arity and __classcell__ validation follow CPython.
- Pattern-matching and import * syntax errors carry the offending line;
  unknown \N{...} names use the codec's message; add_note() names the
  argument type.
- CPython's doctest-based tests run as spec tests through a core-only
  doctest runner, with library-dependent examples rewritten to core code.
- Suspended generators and coroutines are closed when they die; a throw()
  into a generator adds its frame to the traceback at the right line;
  gi_frame of a suspended generator reports the suspension line.
- dir() of generators, coroutines, and async generators lists their methods
  and attributes; builtin slot methods carry CPython's docstrings; code
  objects have CPython's repr.
- spy_collect() runs pending finalizers and frees the rest of the garbage in
  the same call.
- TLA+ specifications (tests/tla) of generator methods, try/with control
  flow, name resolution, and finalization, model-checked with TLC and
  replayed transition by transition on the oracle and spy (make test-tla);
  SpyGC.tla checks spy's memory manager against the language model.
- TLA+ models of integer arithmetic, argument binding, unpacking, method
  resolution order, operator dispatch, attribute access, pattern matching,
  evaluation order, class creation, yield from delegation, async
  generators, except*, the iteration protocol, super(), and dict order.
- tests/tla/coverage.txt maps every section of the 3.15 standard to the
  TLA+ models covering it (make tla-coverage); TLA+ models of numeric and
  string literals, indentation, and line structure.
- A syntax error before a lexer error is reported first, as CPython's
  lexer only reads as far as the parser asks; an indentation error comes
  before its line's DEDENTs; a backslash continuation at the end of the
  source is "unexpected EOF while parsing".
- A name that normalizes to None, True, or False (such as one with a
  full-width letter) raises ValueError at compile time, as in CPython;
  TLA+ model of identifiers.
- f-string replacement fields nested more than two format specifications
  deep are "f-string: expressions nested too deeply"; Interpolation.expression
  leaves out comments. TLA+ models of tokens, f-strings, t-strings, and
  private name mangling complete the lexical analysis chapter.
- TLA+ models of the standard type hierarchy: singletons, object identity,
  numeric types and reprs, sequence operations, mutable sequences, sets,
  and frozendict.
- Function __code__ is writable (checked against the closure's free
  variables) and __builtins__ readable; bound built-in methods have no
  __func__ and __module__ None, method-wrappers and descriptors no
  __module__; a module's __dict__ is read-only and __annotate__ defaults to
  None; deleting a missing attribute reports the object's type. TLA+ models
  of function objects, methods, callables, and module objects.
- A class with several bases reports its layout base as __base__; code
  objects have CPython's co_flags, and co_varnames leaves out cell-only
  locals. TLA+ model of custom classes and instances.
- Code objects have co_names, co_consts (the docstring first), co_code,
  co_linetable, co_stacksize, co_lines(), co_positions(), replace() and
  __replace__, compare and hash by value, and a replaced code assigned to
  __code__ is kept. TLA+ model of code objects.
- Frames: a generator keeps one gi_frame, which reports where it resumes
  or ended (not its def line) and no f_generator once finished; f_lasti,
  f_trace, f_trace_lines, and f_trace_opcodes; f_lineno writes refused
  outside a trace function; frame.clear(); a coroutine frame's f_code.
  TLA+ model of frame objects.
- A slice checks its step before its bounds, and a bound without __index__
  gets CPython's message; tb_frame, tb_lasti, and slice attributes are
  "readonly attribute". TLA+ models of traceback and slice objects.
- A classmethod made by calling classmethod binds any callable (a builtin
  too) as a method object, as types.MethodType does; static and class
  method objects copy only the callable's naming attributes and read its
  annotations on demand; a method over a non-function callable has
  CPython's repr. TLA+ model of static and class method objects.
- A metaclass supplies its classes' unary operators, abs(), format(),
  item assignment and deletion, divmod(), three-argument pow(), next(),
  __getattribute__, and __getattr__; the MRO hook is looked up on the
  metaclass. TLA+ model of special method lookup.
- A data descriptor without __get__ yields to the instance dictionary on
  reads. TLA+ model of descriptor invocation.
- __class__ can be assigned on instances without a __dict__, and between
  classes that add the same slots over the same layout; __slots__ checks
  every name before class variable conflicts. TLA+ model of __slots__.
- Wrong-typed results from __str__, __repr__, __bool__, __format__,
  __bytes__, and __init__ report CPython's messages, naming the class and
  the returned type. TLA+ model of basic customization.
- Class bodies whose methods use __class__ or super() pass a __classcell__
  that type.__new__ fills; a metaclass that drops it or fills it with
  another class raises CPython's RuntimeError or TypeError. TLA+ model of
  metaclass selection.
- TLA+ models of instance and subclass check hooks, __class_getitem__,
  container emulation, and numeric operator dispatch.
- Releasing a memoryview of a __buffer__ exporter (by release(), a with
  block, destruction, or bytes() finishing its copy) calls the exporter's
  __release_buffer__; a non-memoryview __buffer__ result reports CPython's
  message. TLA+ models of the with statement and buffer export.
- Assigning a function's or class's __annotations__ clears __annotate__, a
  callable __annotate__ drops cached annotations, and __annotate__ must be
  callable or None and cannot be deleted. TLA+ model of annotations.
- TypeVarTuple takes bound and variance arguments and has their attributes,
  every PEP 695 type parameter infers variance, ParamSpec has no
  evaluate_bound, and TypeAliasType reports CPython's read-only messages
  and lets __module__ be set. TLA+ models of type parameters and aliases.
- async for, aiter(), with, and async with report CPython 3.15's protocol
  errors, including the hint to use the other kind of with. TLA+ models of
  awaitables, async for, and async with.
- An annotated name declared global or nonlocal (in either order) is a
  SyntaxError, and a name declared both global and nonlocal is reported at
  the first declaration. TLA+ models of scope errors, builtins lookup, and
  dynamic scopes.
- An error raised by an operation in an except handler, a finally block, or
  __exit__ keeps the exception being handled as its __context__ after it
  propagates out (it was created only once the handler had exited). TLA+
  model of the raise statement.
- Interactive (single mode) expression statements call sys.displayhook once
  sys is loaded. TLA+ model of compile modes.
- A None in sys.modules halts an import with ModuleNotFoundError; namespace
  packages have __file__ = None. `lazy import a.b` reifies only a, leaving
  a.b in sys.lazy_modules until looked up; __lazy_modules__ makes the
  module-level imports it lists lazy. TLA+ models of imports and lazy
  imports.
- A relative import whose globals lack __name__ raises KeyError, and a
  non-string __name__ or __package__ raises TypeError with CPython's
  messages. TLA+ model of future statements.
- The error for a ** mapping whose keys() returns a non-iterable omits
  the module builtins or __main__ from the class name. TLA+ models of
  displays and of comprehensions and generator expressions.
- len() and truth testing take a __len__ result through __index__ and
  report it as CPython does; a __bool__ or __contains__ of None raises
  TypeError; `in` on str and bytes reports a wrong left operand with
  CPython's messages. TLA+ models of truth testing and comparisons.
- Unsupported operators on numbers, augmented assignments, `*`, divmod(),
  and three-argument pow() raise CPython's TypeErrors; complex division
  by zero and overflowing complex powers report as CPython does. TLA+
  model of binary arithmetic.
- A subscript index too large for a Py_ssize_t raises "cannot fit 'int'
  into an index-sized integer"; deleting an item without __delitem__
  says "doesn't support item deletion" only for an index into a type with
  sequence methods, as CPython does. TLA+ model of subscriptions.
- A global deleted at module level of exec()'s namespace raises NameError
  when read, not UnboundLocalError. TLA+ model of simple statements.
- sentinel() accepts repr= for the object's representation; its
  __module__ can be set and deleted, and setting __name__ raises
  "readonly attribute", as in CPython. TLA+ models of operator
  precedence and sentinels.
- int.from_bytes() converts only bytes-like objects and iterables, so an
  int or str argument is a TypeError, as is a non-iterable passed to
  bytes() or bytearray() ("cannot convert 'float' object to bytes");
  bytearray() ignores __bytes__. to_bytes() and from_bytes() name a
  non-str byteorder's type, and float.fromhex() rejects a non-str with
  CPython's message. TLA+ models of atoms, grammar, and number methods.
- iter() and for treat __iter__ = None as not iterable, name the type of
  a non-iterable instance, and report an __iter__ that returns a
  non-iterator as "T.__iter__() must return an iterator, not U". TLA+
  models of numeric hashing and iterators.
- Setting or deleting a range's start, stop, or step raises "readonly
  attribute"; range.index() reports a miss as CPython does; len() of a
  range beyond sys.maxsize raises CPython's OverflowError. TLA+ model of
  ranges.
- str methods word bad arguments as CPython does: split's "must be str
  or None", strip's "strip arg must be None or str", startswith's
  tuple messages, find's "find() argument 1 must be str", search bounds'
  "slice indices must be integers...", the fill character's type,
  removeprefix, join of a non-iterable, maketrans, and the encoding and
  errors arguments of encode, decode, str(), bytes(), and bytearray().
  splitlines() takes any object for keepends. A builtin method given
  keywords it does not take names itself by qualified name
  ("list.append() takes no keyword arguments"). TLA+ model of str.
- bytes %s and %b format any buffer, a memoryview included. TLA+ models
  of format specifications and printf-style formatting.
- bytes.isupper() and bytearray.isupper() hold for uppercase letters
  (bytes have no titlecase); bytes and bytearray padding accept either
  type as the fill byte, with CPython's errors; hex() reports a
  separator's length before its ASCII-ness and a non-str one as having
  no len(); fromhex() reports a final lone digit as an odd count. TLA+
  model of bytes and bytearray.
- set.intersection(), intersection_update(), and issubset() with an
  iterable, and a dict items view & a set, report an unhashable item as
  CPython does, without naming it a set element. TLA+ model of dict
  methods and views.
- TLA+ model of GenericAlias and Union: alias attributes, substitution,
  and union flattening, deduplication, and isinstance().
- int() and float() accept bytearray, memoryview, and other buffers, as
  CPython does, and word other argument types' errors as CPython does;
  float() parses strings longer than 4096 characters. TLA+ model of the
  integer string conversion length limit.
- NoneType, NotImplementedType, and the ellipsis type reject arguments
  with CPython's "takes no arguments" message. TLA+ model of the built-in
  constants and the targets they may not occupy.
- complex() parses a string only as its sole positional argument and
  names the offending argument and type in its errors, as CPython does.
  TLA+ model of the numeric built-in functions.
- TLA+ model of the iteration and sorting built-in functions.
- type() with three arguments names the argument of the wrong type, and
  dir() reports a non-iterable __dir__ result as list() would. TLA+ model
  of the object built-in functions.
- chr() takes __index__ values and reports one too big for a C long as
  out of range. TLA+ model of the text built-in functions.
- exec() and eval() word bad globals and locals as CPython does, naming
  the type for exec() and suggesting a dict for an eval() mapping. TLA+
  model of compile(), eval(), exec(), and their namespaces.
- TLA+ models of the built-in exception hierarchy, exception objects, and
  the concrete exceptions.
- Comprehensions report an unbound local of their function as
  UnboundLocalError; finalizers run depth first; str length, slicing, and
  find() no longer rescan the string.
- The Python binding is now the small-python package in python/ (import
  small_python), merged with the small-python PyPI project: uv lockfile,
  release script, PyPI publish workflow with cibuildwheel wheels for Linux and
  macOS, a standalone sdist carrying the engine sources, and user
  documentation in python/docs.
- small_python fixes: integers beyond 4,300 digits, Object len/in/==/hash/dir,
  engine-first attributes, protocol exceptions (KeyError, IndexError,
  TypeError), next() on non-iterators (previously read invalid memory), host
  exceptions matched to builtins only and kept as the Error's __cause__,
  KeyboardInterrupt and SystemExit passed through, del rt[name] no longer
  resetting the step count, re-entry refused from output and loader and from
  other threads, and close() releasing host callables. Tests in python/tests
  (98 cases, also run under ASan and UBSan) and a type stub.
